EXTRA = {
"google-eat-here-domains-orange-county": [
 ("How redirects should work", "<p>If you use a new ending as a campaign address, point it at a specific page with a permanent redirect, for example yourname.eat sending visitors straight to your menu page. Do not build a second copy of your website on the new domain; duplicate sites split attention and confuse customers and search engines.</p>"),
 ("What it costs to hold a domain", "<p>Google says the new endings will have a base annual rate once public, and Early Access prices fall each day until November 17. Factor renewal into the decision: a domain you stop renewing can be registered by someone else, so only buy names you are willing to keep.</p>")],
"gemini-task-automation-bookings-anaheim": [
 ("A worked example: an Anaheim restaurant", "<p>Imagine a family visiting the Disneyland Resort asks Gemini on their phone to book a table for four near the Anaheim Convention Center at seven. If one restaurant nearby is listed on a reservation app with accurate hours and availability and another only takes phone calls, the assistant can complete the booking with the first one. The second restaurant may be just as good, but it is harder to choose automatically.</p>"),
 ("A worked example: an Orange County salon", "<p>A salon in Orange with online booking that lists every service, stylist and price can be booked by a customer, or an assistant acting for them, at midnight. A salon whose booking page lists only half its services, or shows last year's prices, risks failed bookings and frustrated customers. Keeping the booking system as accurate as the website matters.</p>"),
 ("Questions to ask your booking provider", "<ul><li>Which apps and assistants can book through your system?</li><li>How quickly do changes to hours or services sync?</li><li>Can customers book without creating an account?</li><li>How are cancellations and deposits handled?</li><li>What reporting shows where bookings came from?</li></ul>"),
 ("Privacy and trust", "<p>Customers trust assistants to act for them only when the result is reliable. Clear policies on cancellations, deposits and refunds, shown in your booking listings, reduce disputes and make your business a safer choice for both people and AI agents.</p>")],
"google-holiday-100-orange-county-retailers": [
 ("A worked example: a Costa Mesa boutique", "<p>A Costa Mesa boutique notices utility jackets and kitten heels on Google's list and already stocks both. It rewrites the two product pages with sizes, materials and styling notes, checks that its Merchant Center feed shows the right price and stock, adds a line about same-day pickup and posts photos of the items on its Business Profile. Shoppers searching for those trends now have a reason to choose a local store.</p>"),
 ("Writing product descriptions that work", "<p>Good descriptions answer the questions a shopper would ask a salesperson: what it is made of, how it fits, how to care for it, what it pairs with and why it makes a good gift. Avoid copying manufacturer text word for word; specific, original detail helps both shoppers and AI shopping tools understand your product.</p>"),
 ("Gift guides that earn links", "<p>A local gift guide can earn links and mentions from neighborhood newsletters and community groups if it is genuinely useful, such as gifts from Orange County makers or gifts under a set price. Mentions from local sources help Google understand how well-known your store is.</p>"),
 ("Returns and holiday policies", "<p>Holiday shoppers want to know about gift receipts, extended return windows and delivery cut-off dates. State them clearly on product pages and in your listings; clear policies remove a common reason shoppers hesitate.</p>"),
 ("After the holidays", "<p>Keep trend pages updated rather than deleting them; many trends carry into the new year, and an established page with reviews is easier to rank again next season.</p>"),
 ("Using trends year round", "<p>The Holiday 100 is one snapshot, but the habit it teaches is useful all year: watch what people search for, compare it with what you stock and update pages before demand peaks. Google Trends and your own Search Console data show the same signals for your products and your area.</p>")],
"google-search-profiles-local-brands": [
 ("A worked example: an Anaheim food creator", "<p>A food creator in Anaheim with 12,000 Instagram followers and a YouTube channel reviewing local restaurants now meets Google's threshold. A Search profile brings their videos, social accounts and articles together on Google, and if Google's AI Mode test expands, their name could appear as a link on video results about Anaheim dining.</p>"),
 ("A worked example: a local media group", "<p>A small Orange County media company that runs a city newsletter and two neighborhood sites can now manage all three Search profiles from one login with multi-account support, keeping each brand's latest articles and links current.</p>"),
 ("Profiles and local businesses together", "<p>A business that also publishes, such as a restaurant group with a popular cooking channel, may benefit from both a Google Business Profile for its locations and a Search profile for its content. Keep the names and descriptions aligned so it is clear they belong to the same brand.</p>"),
 ("Building toward eligibility", "<p>If you are below 10,000 followers, focus on the platform your customers actually use, publish consistently and engage genuinely with local audiences. Audience growth through real content also supports your reviews, links and visibility in AI answers.</p>"),
 ("What to put on the profile", "<ul><li>Your official name exactly as used elsewhere.</li><li>A short, specific description of what you cover.</li><li>Links to your website and active social accounts.</li><li>Your latest articles or videos.</li></ul>")],
"google-october-2026-ai-updates-local-business": [
 ("What Genie 4 means for marketing", "<p>Genie 4 is aimed at interactive simulations and at training environments for robots and AI agents rather than at local marketing. It is worth knowing about, but it does not change what an Orange County business should publish this month.</p>"),
 ("AI images on your website", "<p>Many businesses now use AI tools to create illustrations. That is fine when it is honest: label illustrative images clearly, use real photos for your team, premises and work, and never use AI images to depict results you did not deliver. As detection tools such as SynthID spread, transparency protects your credibility.</p>"),
 ("Preparing for agents that act", "<p>Alongside stronger models, Google is adding features that let AI act for people, such as Gemini task automation on Android. Businesses that are bookable online with accurate details are better placed as assistants take on more tasks.</p>"),
 ("A worked example", "<p>An Orange County plumbing company checks what Google's AI features say about it after the update and finds an old phone number repeated from a directory. It fixes the directory, updates its Business Profile and adds a clear contact page. The next month, the AI answer shows the right number. Small fixes like this are the most practical response to model updates.</p>")],
}
